# Fridge dual-track architecture run

## Result

- Preview: `tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/stage-fridge-arch-preview.png`
- Local final: `tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/stage-fridge-arch-final.png`
- Cloud final: `tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/stage-fridge-arch-final-cloud.png`
- Comparison: `tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/arch-vs-ref.png`
- Metrics: `tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/arch-metrics.json`

The comparison resizes all inputs to the same height and does not paste the raw
high-resolution reference. The active `white` environment uses the flat white
world and skips HDRI loading. The final camera restores the `C@R@C^T` rotation
conversion and retains the Blender camera-basis/roll correction required by the
Blender camera object.

## Commands

```bash
python3 tools/dual-track/run_dual_track.py both \
  --scene tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/stage-fridge-scene_snapshot.json \
  --asset-map tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/stage-fridge-assets.json \
  --assets-root tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/assets \
  --view 298cfe60-923d-44fb-a0d1-f2206b9a48e1 \
  --preview-out tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/stage-fridge-arch-preview.png \
  --final-out tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/stage-fridge-arch-final.png \
  --compare-out tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/arch-vs-ref.png \
  --ref tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/ref/fridge-ref-front-329c-1024.png \
  --metrics-out tools/cloud-service/poc-out/fridge/arch-metrics.json \
  --preview-width 960 --preview-height 540 --preview-spp 32 \
  --final-width 960 --final-height 540 --final-spp 64
```

## Timings

| Track | Wall-clock |
| --- | ---: |
| Local preview, 32 spp | 10.07 s |
| Local Blender final, 64 spp | 21.08 s |
| Cloud Blender final, 64 spp | approximately 40 s, including upload/import |

## Metrics

```json
{
  "brightness_std": {
    "preview": 43.934568475230556,
    "final": 4.974114430161699,
    "ref": 42.81089388887461
  },
  "silhouette_iou_preview_vs_ref": 0.8004316040881151,
  "silhouette_iou_final_vs_ref": 0.037288977826723434,
  "threshold": 16
}
```

Silhouettes are background-difference masks, not raw brightness thresholds, so
they compare product coverage rather than white background.

## Cloud

The cloud render succeeded at `ubuntu@43.192.32.90:/tmp/mutracer-final/` with
headless Blender `/usr/local/bin/blender` (4.2.23 LTS). The scripts, scene,
asset map, and 436 required assets were uploaded. Asset-map values were remapped
to their keys for the temporary remote layout, and the resulting PNG was pulled
to the path above.

## Gap versus gold

Final framing is restored, but flat white ambient washing removes product
contrast and most product-mask coverage (`brightness_std` 4.97 versus gold
42.81; final-vs-reference IoU 0.037).
    scene.camera = camera_object
    scene.render.resolution_x = render_width
    scene.render.resolution_y = render_height

environment_id = view.get("active_environment")
environment = (stage_scene.get("environments") or {}).get(environment_id)
environment_texture_path = None
environment_settings = (environment or {}).get("settings") or {}
background_type = environment_settings.get("background_type", "white")
if background_type != "white":
    texture_id = environment_settings.get("image")
    texture = (stage_scene.get("textures") or {}).get(texture_id)
    texture_url = texture and (texture.get("urls") or texture.get("url"))
    environment_texture_path = assets.get(texture_url)

scene.render.film_transparent = False
world = bpy.data.worlds.new("world")
scene.world = world
world.use_nodes = True
background = world.node_tree.nodes["Background"]
if background_type == "white":
    # The stage white studio is a pure white backdrop; preview renders it through
    # background_intensity, so Blender keeps the same flat white here.
    background.inputs["Color"].default_value = (1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0)
    background.inputs["Strength"].default_value = 1.0
elif environment_texture_path and os.path.isfile(environment_texture_path):
    environment_texture = world.node_tree.nodes.new("ShaderNodeTexEnvironment")
    environment_texture.image = bpy.data.images.load(environment_texture_path)
    world.node_tree.links.new(
        environment_texture.outputs["Color"], background.inputs["Color"]
    )
    hdri_brightness = float(environment_settings.get("hdri_brightness", 1))
    background.inputs["Strength"].default_value = min(hdri_brightness, 10.0)
else:
    background.inputs["Color"].default_value = (0.95, 0.95, 0.95, 1)
    background.inputs["Strength"].default_value = 1.0

scene.render.engine = "CYCLES"
preferences = bpy.context.preferences.addons["cycles"].preferences
preferred_devices = ("METAL", "OPTIX", "CUDA") if sys.platform == "darwin" else (
    "OPTIX",
    "CUDA",
)
for device_type in preferred_devices:
    try:
        preferences.compute_device_type = device_type
        preferences.get_devices()
        gpu_count = 0
        for device in preferences.devices:
            device.use = device.type != "CPU"
            gpu_count += 1 if device.use else 0
        if gpu_count:
            scene.cycles.device = "GPU"
            print(f"[gpu] {device_type}: {gpu_count}", flush=True)
            break
    except Exception as error:
        print(f"[gpu] {device_type} unavailable: {error}", flush=True)
else:
    scene.cycles.device = "CPU"

scene.cycles.samples = spp
scene.cycles.use_denoising = denoise
scene.render.image_settings.file_format = "PNG"
scene.render.filepath = out_path
bpy.ops.render.render(write_still=True)
print(f"[done] {out_path}", flush=True)

